# GTFS Static — Design Rules

## Data model (`internal/models/gtfs.go`)

- `StopTime` times: **`int32` seconds-past-midnight** — never `time.Time` (supports ≥24:00, 4 B vs 24 B)
- `Trip.StopTimes`: **contiguous slice sorted by `Sequence`** — routing scans forward only
- Hot-path structs: **flat fields**, no pointer indirection inside inner loops
- `TransitGraph`: `map[string]*T` for O(1) ID lookup at parse/query setup time

## Parser (`internal/gtfs/parser.go`)

- **Stdlib only** — no external CSV/zip libraries
- `zip.OpenReader` + O(1) file index; `csv.Reader` with `ReuseRecord = true`
- Pre-size maps: stops `8192`, routes `512`, trips `32768`
- Custom `parseGTFSTime` — handles `25:30:00`; faster than `time.Parse`
- Orphan `stop_times` (missing trip): **skip**, don't hard-fail
- Post-parse: sort every trip's `StopTimes` by `Sequence`

## Parse order

`stops.txt` → `routes.txt` → `trips.txt` → `stop_times.txt`

## When extending

- New static fields: add to `models` first, then parser; preserve allocation patterns
- Preprocessing for routing belongs in `internal/router/`, not parser — parser only builds `TransitGraph`
